  "detourRule": "tiers are tried in order: 'band' is the declared +/-12 m respawn band with the 2.276 m band (1.676 m car + 0.30 m margin per side); 'wide' is a +/-24 m window with the same band (a new course); 'narrow' is the +/-24 m window with the 1.680 m band (the documented car width, no safety margin; a design choice, not a recovered retail hull). A later tier is only attempted when the previous one has a station with no band-clear lateral position (or no continuous detour). A tier succeeds only when the whole detoured line is band-clear and continuous (<= 0.5 m between consecutive samples); a station whose racing point is not clear moves along its own normal to the nearest continuous band-clear position in the tier window (0.25 m steps) and the line returns to the racing line when the racing point becomes clear",
